## F32 cause

The hint was a separate root overlay above the entire deck, rather than part of the moving document/page. Its only update was in status refresh and it examined the current editor. When an empty selected note exposed a nonempty neighbour during a drag/slide, the current editor was still empty: the overlay remained above the neighbour's text. Carousel motion had no hint invalidation/suppression path. New appearance contexts also defaulted to a visible hint until a later status update. The fix makes the bound document authoritative, defaults the overlay to hidden, refreshes explicitly on binding/appearance/text paths, and hides it for motion. The screenshot's precise original input sequence was not replayed; the concrete empty-source/nonempty-preview failure path is now a regression check.

## Verification

Prescribed command-only quit was run before each build from `src/AntiQuickPad`. Final Release/no-restore/no-shared-compilation build: **0 warnings / 0 errors**. [Build log](../../docs/design/m6/built/build-T014.log). No process was killed.

The retained Classic suite remains enabled, including persistence, command-only quit, save-failure, single-instance and measurement smoke. Its carousel waits were increased from 300 to 450 ms for the new 280 ms animation plus callback scheduling. Shared pixel proof helpers now accept an optional palette; default callers retain the original checks. Active-guide pixels require the palette's intended direction (darker on light, brighter on dark), and are isolated from the separate caret-row renderer. Strike coverage uses absolute luminance-channel distance on light palettes; original geometry/outside-pixel tolerances remain.

All 40 requested real production state/scale renders were regenerated and viewed in four labelled contact sheets; full-size main and all menu/fold close-ups were also inspected. Eight fold-hover state renders, eight close-ups and four six-level heading proofs supplement the original 40. [Gallery](../../docs/design/m6/built/README.md), [manifest](../../docs/design/m6/built/manifest.json). These are actual production resident/editor trees with isolated notes. Contact-sheet assembly is for inspection only; original PNGs remain the direct Avalonia renders.


